WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.821
Individual researchers
cannot carry RRI alone.

2
00:00:04.101 --> 00:00:07.791
Institutions shape what is
rewarded, resourced and expected.

3
00:00:08.071 --> 00:00:09.373
Here are six levers.

4
00:00:10.573 --> 00:00:11.810
First, governance.

5
00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:17.991
Embed RRI in research strategy, ethics
policies and quality assurance, link it to

6
00:00:17.991 --> 00:00:22.799
institutional values, and appoint
RRI champions or working groups.

7
00:00:23.999 --> 00:00:25.578
Second, structural tools.

8
00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:30.869
Provide checklists, planning templates
and guidance, use a theory of change to

9
00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:36.009
connect research outcomes with societal
impact, and support open access and data

10
00:00:36.009 --> 00:00:37.037
ethics policies.

11
00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:41.349
Keep these tools visible and
usable, not abstract or burdensome.

12
00:00:42.549 --> 00:00:44.149
Third, capacity building.

13
00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:49.927
Offer training, workshops and mentoring,
and recognise RRI in performance reviews,

14
00:00:49.927 --> 00:00:51.938
career development and awards.

15
00:00:53.138 --> 00:00:55.122
Fourth, diversity and inclusion.

16
00:00:55.402 --> 00:01:00.853
Align RRI with Gender Equality Plans
and with diversity, equity and inclusion

17
00:01:00.853 --> 00:01:01.631
strategies.

18
00:01:01.911 --> 00:01:05.623
Both aim to make research more
equitable, inclusive and just.

19
00:01:06.823 --> 00:01:12.255
Fifth, monitor progress with indicators
and self-assessments, such as the RRI Tools

20
00:01:12.255 --> 00:01:13.629
self-reflection tool.

21
00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:18.698
And sixth, nurture a culture of openness,
where teams can reflect, talk across

22
00:01:18.698 --> 00:01:21.461
disciplines, and learn
from ethical missteps.

23
00:01:22.661 --> 00:01:28.526
For example, a university can include
RRI as a standard criterion in all of its

24
00:01:28.526 --> 00:01:32.090
internal funding calls
and proposal evaluations.

25
00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.975
The goal is a cultural shift.

26
00:01:35.255 --> 00:01:40.604
Responsibility becomes embedded not just
in policies, but in everyday conversations

27
00:01:40.604 --> 00:01:41.506
and decisions.

28
00:01:42.706 --> 00:01:44.050
Thank you for watching.

29
00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:47.850
Continue with the module to
put these ideas into practice.
